From: Yves Bicker <yves_bicker@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:51:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] [MORALGYM] distill only the response tokens after a
 marker

New self_distillation.distill_after (default null). When set, the SDPO
loss covers only the tokens after the last occurrence of the marker in
each response, e.g. "</think>": a reasoning model's thinking still
conditions student and teacher but receives no gradient. Responses
without the marker contribute no loss. Logs the distilled-token and
marker-found fractions. The marker is matched on token pieces, so a
multi-token marker (Olmo-3) works like a single-token one (Qwen3).
---
